54,3,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
55,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"We have Market Plaza, Woodland Walk, Wetland Restoration, and Sports Terraces. I lean toward the Wetlands.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Misaki,,The Wetlands involve significant earth-moving. The Market Plaza is safer for the soil.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Market Plaza is affordable to maintain, but we can't use the habitat fund for it.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Sports Terraces fit our volunteer base, but the maintenance costs for courts are high.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Minako,,"Wetland Restoration solves the drainage and heat issues, and fits the funding.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, the earlier programme showed the overflow basin was the only thing that lasted.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, but the Wetland plan is a massive dig. The clay subsoil is a nightmare.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Mio,,"If we go with Woodland Walk, the upkeep is triple the cost of a plaza.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Asuka,,We have habitat volunteers who could help with the Wetlands or Woodland Walk.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Minako,,The tram commuters need a clear path. Wetlands with boardwalks could work.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,I'm convinced by the durability of the water-based works. I vote Wetland Restoration.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"I still fear the slippage, but the Market Plaza is too boring for the fund. I'll go Wetlands.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Mio,,"I hate the upkeep costs, but if the fund pays the capital, I can live with it. Wetlands.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Asuka,,The volunteer alignment makes the Wetlands a strong choice. I vote for that.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Minako,,"It solves the drainage, the heat, and the funding. Wetland Restoration it is.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
